# Real code

## Recall

Of each tool's findings, how many zanity reports on the same lines with a mapped rule.

| Tool | Its rule | zanity rule | Note | Its findings | zanity too | Recall |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| testdesiderata | `DET001` | `nondeterministic-test` |  | 35 | 35 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| testdesiderata | `ISO003` | `filesystem-in-test` | zanity reports reads and writes of real paths, not of the test's own temporary directory | 64 | 6 | [9%]($text.attrs('badge','partial')) |
| testdesiderata | `ISO006` | `unmanaged-temp-in-test` |  | 2 | 2 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| testdesiderata | `ISO008` | `process-in-test` |  | 5 | 5 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| testdesiderata | `RDL002` | `undocumented-test` |  | 3 | 3 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| testdesiderata | `SPC001` | `generic-catch`, `swallowed-error` |  | 2 | 2 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |
| testdesiderata | `SPC002` | `opaque-check`, `assertion-message` |  | 16 | 16 | [100%]($text.attrs('badge','pass')) |

## Agreement

Of zanity's findings, how many the tool also reports. Low agreement is zanity finding what the tool doesn't, which can be either tool's mistake.

